1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,580
Open Food Facts tags these Plant-Based Puffs as vegan.

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:08,210
The FDA says they tested positive for milk.

3
00:00:08,328 --> 00:00:10,928
A shopper with a milk allergy could trust that tag.

4
00:00:11,668 --> 00:00:15,108
ClearShelf holds the listing automatically, cites every reason,

5
00:00:15,428 --> 00:00:18,398
and clears nothing without the compliance officer's signature.

6
00:00:22,129 --> 00:00:25,159
The officer pastes a barcode and picks the UK.

7
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:30,937
Each step streams as the local Nemotron model plans it:

8
00:00:31,217 --> 00:00:33,057
the product row, the recall notice,

9
00:00:33,417 --> 00:00:34,817
the data-quality gate, memory.

10
00:00:35,417 --> 00:00:37,507
Every read goes through Zetaris.

11
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,500
Zetaris joins the three sources in one

12
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,280
semantic layer with 22 data-quality rules;

13
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,750
a failed rule holds the listing.

14
00:00:48,567 --> 00:00:50,627
The result: HOLD, applied automatically,

15
00:00:50,647 --> 00:00:52,407
since holding needs no signature.

16
00:00:52,987 --> 00:00:57,450
Each chip opens its evidence: the exact Lightning SQL,

17
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,977
the source, the licence and the cache time.

18
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:04,080
Why was this held?

19
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:07,740
Five plain lines: the recall, the missing ingredient list,

20
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,800
and the vegan claim that milk contradicts,

21
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,390
each with its evidence.

22
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:14,913
On this dark chocolate, a keyword rule reads milk in

23
00:01:14,933 --> 00:01:17,653
cocoa butter and treats "may contain" as "contains".

24
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:20,573
Both readers, Nemotron and the verifier,

25
00:01:20,593 --> 00:01:22,443
call these "may contain".

26
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,100
Clearing always needs the officer:

27
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,220
the form shows what will be signed,

28
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:29,700
the server issues a single-use contract,

29
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:32,150
and only then is the decision written.

30
00:01:37,567 --> 00:01:40,117
Zetaris reads the signed row straight back.

31
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:43,887
The recall watch can replay a known past:

32
00:01:43,907 --> 00:01:47,427
as of 10 October it sees only notices reported by then,

33
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,050
and a banner says so.

34
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,580
Polling to today, new notices arrive and

35
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,220
a bounded investigation runs:

36
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:56,380
each Markovian step carries a small state forward,

37
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:58,250
so the prompt stays flat.

38
00:01:58,433 --> 00:02:00,173
Paused on two of Nemotron's notes.

39
00:02:00,693 --> 00:02:02,653
It picks each step from the host's checklist:

40
00:02:03,113 --> 00:02:06,293
check the FDA recall for this barcode,

41
00:02:06,453 --> 00:02:07,633
then parse the notice found,

42
00:02:07,653 --> 00:02:10,303
to confirm the barcode and the allergen.

43
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:14,313
An FDA notice names this cake's barcode exactly.

44
00:02:14,973 --> 00:02:16,433
It's a US-only recall,

45
00:02:16,693 --> 00:02:20,113
so the UK listing is held automatically, with the reason.

46
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:22,863
Name-only matches wait for a person.

47
00:02:23,433 --> 00:02:26,733
Contradictions are queued, never settled by the last write.

48
00:02:27,233 --> 00:02:29,753
The officer resolves the milk conflict with a reason,

49
00:02:29,773 --> 00:02:32,083
and the ledger records who decided.

50
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:42,040
Zetaris is the only data path, and its SQL is the citation.

51
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,820
Meterless engines run the loop, the memory and the world model;

52
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:48,640
the signed contracts follow Meterless Scout's spec.

53
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,670
Nemotron runs on one local GPU.

54
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,473
Measured: ten of ten scenarios pass;

55
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:57,593
in ten replayed recall polls,

56
00:02:57,853 --> 00:03:01,553
the matched listing was held in a median of 68.4 seconds;

57
00:03:01,813 --> 00:03:03,523
and nothing clears unsigned.

58
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:06,940
ClearShelf.

59
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:10,310
Every decision is cited, and every release is signed.

60
00:03:10,415 --> 00:03:12,125
A solo entry from Singapore.
